course: dictionary
lesson: 14646
title: A word with three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. Precipitant is a word with three meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. Look for clues: is there a liquid and a science test, a sudden event, or a rushed choice?
explain: In science, a precipitant is a substance you add to a liquid so that solid bits form and sink out of it. «The teacher added a precipitant to the cloudy water, and a white powder slowly sank to the bottom.» The clues are water and powder, so this is the science meaning.
explain: In formal writing, a precipitant is a trigger, the thing that starts something suddenly. «A loud bang was the precipitant of the panic in the playground.» The bang started the panic, so the bang is the precipitant.
explain: As an adjective, precipitant is rare and formal. «He made a precipitant decision and jumped into the lake without checking the depth.» It means done too quickly, without thinking. Check by swapping in rushed: a rushed decision fits, so the meaning is right.
fact: Precipitant is mainly a noun, and as an adjective it is rare and formal.
fact: «Precipitant» means a substance that makes solid bits come out of a liquid, in science.
fact: «Precipitant» also means a trigger: something that causes an event to happen suddenly.
fact: As an adjective, «precipitant» means done too quickly, without thinking; rushed.
fact: Phrases to notice: «add a precipitant», «the precipitant of», and «a precipitant decision».
exercise: «The teacher added a precipitant to the cloudy water.» In this sentence, what is a precipitant? | A kind of cloud | *A substance that makes solid bits form and sink | A rushed decision made in a hurry | A loud noise that starts a fight
exercise: «Stress was the precipitant of the argument.» What does precipitant mean here? | A container for water | A slow and careful plan | *The trigger that made the argument start suddenly | A liquid that stops arguments
exercise: «He made a precipitant decision and jumped in without looking.» What does precipitant mean? | *Done too quickly, without thinking | Kind and gentle | Carefully planned for weeks | Made of metal
test: «The loud bang was the precipitant of the panic.» What is the bang? | A quiet whisper | A liquid used in a science test | *The trigger that started the panic | A rushed decision
test: Which phrase uses precipitant as an adjective, meaning rushed? | add a precipitant | a clear glass bottle | the precipitant of the rain | *a precipitant decision
exam: Jayden says precipitant is a long word he will never need. Why might he be wrong? | It only means a kind of cloud, so it is useless | Nobody ever writes it down | Long words are never useful | *It appears in science and formal writing, so knowing it helps him understand those texts
